{
  "info": {
    "name": "PanelScan API — Auth Module",
    "description": "Register, login, /me, refresh-token rotation, and logout. Also includes a small Rate Limiting folder demonstrating the 5-requests-per-15-minutes-per-IP limit shared by /register, /login, and /refresh (only enforced when NODE_ENV is development/production — the automated test suite runs with NODE_ENV=test, where both rate limiters are deliberately disabled). Follows the same per-module-collection pattern as every other PanelScan-*.postman_collection.json file.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000/api" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "register"] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firstName\": \"Juan\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Dela Cruz\",\n  \"email\": \"juan.auth@panelscan.test\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd123\",\n  \"phone\": \"+63 912 345 6789\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Register only issues an access token, not a refresh token - log in",
                  "// separately (below) to obtain one and start a refreshable session.",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"juan.auth@panelscan.test\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd123\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  var data = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', data.token);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', data.refreshToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Me",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "refresh"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}" }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Rotation: this refresh token is now revoked; both stored values must",
                  "// be replaced with the new pair returned here, or the next call 401s.",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  var data = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', data.token);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', data.refreshToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "logout"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}" }
          },
          "description": "Revokes only this one refresh token - other devices/sessions for the same user are untouched. Run 'Refresh' again afterward with the same {{refreshToken}} to see it correctly return 401 ('has been revoked')."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Rate Limiting (manual verification)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login x6 rapidly - 6th call returns 429",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"nobody@panelscan.test\",\n  \"password\": \"WrongPassword123\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "description": "POST /auth/register + /auth/login + /auth/refresh share ONE 5-requests-per-15-minutes-per-IP counter (RATE_LIMIT_AUTH_MAX / RATE_LIMIT_AUTH_WINDOW_MS). Use Postman's Runner (or the 'Send' button, 6 times fast) against a server started with `npm run dev` (NODE_ENV=development) to see the 6th response come back 429 with `{ \"success\": false, \"message\": \"Too many authentication attempts. Please try again later.\" }` and `RateLimit-*` response headers. This will NOT trigger against a server running under NODE_ENV=test - both rate limiters are deliberately disabled there so the ~530-test automated suite isn't throttled; see tests/rateLimit/rateLimit.test.ts for the isolated, fully-enforcing test coverage of this behavior instead."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
